.grimp_cache
.vscode
.venv
.agents
skills-lock.json
.claude/*
# The enforcement layer IS the gate for agent-authored code, so it is version
# controlled: a hook that only exists on one laptop protects nothing and does
# not survive a clone. Skills and workflows are that same layer -- run-merge-train's
# lane rules and process-issues' HOUSE rules decide what agents may ship -- so they
# are tracked too. Only per-machine config (settings.local.json: permissions and
# MCP toggles, not policy) stays out.
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/workflows/
# A stray browser download: byte-identical to .claude/skills/wizard/SKILL.md, but named
# .yaml, so check-yaml reads its `---` frontmatter as two documents and fails. Left on
# disk rather than deleted -- it is not this change's to remove -- but never tracked.
.claude/skills/openai (3).yaml
AGENTS.md
.codegraph
# local analysis scratch (not committed)
.scratch/
evaluation/results/.judge_cache/
.sonar
# CLAUDE.md is the agent contract (container-not-host, no-silent-fallback, the
# gate layout). Ignoring it is how this repo ended up with a CLAUDE.md
# describing an entirely different project -- so it is tracked, and the rule that
# ignored it anyway five lines below this comment is gone.
.mcp.json

graphify-out
prototypes
.scratch*
# Candidate ontologies under evaluation — not part of the shipped bundle.
# Scoped to `candidates/` on purpose: hatchling drops VCS-ignored files from the
# wheel, so a broader `assets/` rule would silently unship cco/cco.json, which
# `GraphKnowsSettings.ontology_source` defaults to.
# The path moved with the package (frames/ + ontology/ -> symbolic/). A stale
# path here fails SILENTLY: the files simply stop being ignored, get swept in
# by `git add graphknows/`, and the large-file hook then rejects the whole
# commit on a 4.6 MB .owl that was never meant to be committed.
graphknows/symbolic/ontology/assets/cco-extensions/candidates/
